## RIGHTS OF PERSONS WITH DISABILITIES

## Part One

General

#### Article 43

Persons with Disabilities have the right to:
a. life;
b. freedom from stigma;
c. privacy;
d. justice and legal protection;
e. education;
f. employment, entrepreneurship, and cooperatives;
g. health;
h. politics;
i. religion;
j. sports;
k. culture and tourism;
l. social welfare;
m. accessibility;
n. Public services;
o. protection from disasters;
p. habilitation and rehabilitation;
q. concessions;
r. data collection;

s. live independently and be included in society; t. express themselves, communicate, and obtain information; u. move and citizenship; and
v. freedom from acts of Discrimination, neglect, torture, and exploitation.

#### Article 44

In addition to the rights of Persons with Disabilities as referred to in paragraph (1), women with disabilities have the right to:
a. reproductive health;
b. accept or refuse the use of contraceptives;
c. obtain greater Protection from multiple Discrimination;
d. obtain greater Protection from acts of violence, including sexual violence and exploitation.

#### Article 45

In addition to the rights of Persons with Disabilities as referred to in paragraph (1), children with disabilities have the right to:
a. obtain special Protection from Discrimination, neglect, harassment, exploitation, as well as sexual violence and crimes; b. obtain family care and upbringing or substitute family for optimal growth and development;
c. have their interests protected in decision-making; d. treatment of children in a humane manner in accordance with the dignity and rights of the child;
e. fulfillment of special needs;
f. equal treatment with other children to achieve social integration and individual development; andg. obtain social assistance.

## Part Two

Right to Life

#### Article 46

The right to life for Persons with Disabilities includes the right to:
a. respect for integrity;
b. not be deprived of life;
c. obtain care and upbringing that ensures their survival;
d. freedom from neglect, shackling, confinement, and isolation; e. freedom from threats and various forms of exploitation; and f. freedom from torture, other cruel, inhuman, and degrading treatment and punishment.

## Part Three

Right to Freedom from Stigma

#### Article 47

The right to freedom from stigma for Persons with Disabilities includes the right to freedom from harassment, insult, and negative labeling related to their disability condition.

Part Four Right to Privacy

#### Article 48

The right to privacy for Persons with Disabilities includes the right to:
a. be recognized as a human person who can demand and obtain equal treatment and Protection in accordance with human dignity in public;
b. form a family and continue descendants through a valid marriage;
c. respect for home and family;
d. obtain Protection of personal and family life; and e. have the confidentiality of personal data, correspondence, and other forms of personal communication protected, including health data and information.

Part Five Right to Justice and Legal Protection

#### Article 49

The right to justice and legal protection for Persons with Disabilities includes the right to:
a. equal treatment before the law;
b. be recognized as a legal subject;
